@startuml RAG_Lifecycle
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #E1F5FE
  BorderColor #0277BD
  FontSize 12
  FontColor #263238
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF9C4
  DiamondBorderColor #F57F17
}

title End-to-End RAG (Retrieval Augmented Generation) Lifecycle

start

:**1. Problem Definition & Scope**
----
* Define RAG use case
  (Q&A, Document Search,
   Knowledge Base, Support Bot)
* Identify knowledge domain
* Define data sources
* Set accuracy requirements
* Define latency constraints
* Determine scale needs
* Plan budget and resources
* Set success metrics
  (Relevance, Accuracy, Coverage);

:**2. Data Source Identification**
----
* Identify document sources:
  - Internal documents (PDFs, Docs)
  - Databases
  - Knowledge bases
  - Web content
  - APIs
  - Wikis
  - Code repositories
  - Spreadsheets
* Assess data volume
* Check data accessibility
* Review data rights/licenses
* Identify update frequency
* Document data lineage;

:**3. Document Collection & Ingestion**
----
* Set up data connectors
* Extract documents:
  - PDF extraction
  - HTML scraping
  - API calls
  - Database queries
  - File system scanning
* Handle different formats:
  - Text files
  - PDFs
  - Word documents
  - HTML/Markdown
  - JSON/XML
  - Images (OCR if needed)
* Store raw documents
* Track document metadata
* Version control documents;

:**4. Document Preprocessing**
----
* Extract text content
* Remove boilerplate
  (Headers, footers, navigation)
* Clean text:
  - Remove special characters
  - Fix encoding issues
  - Normalize whitespace
  - Handle line breaks
* Remove duplicate content
* Handle multi-language content
* Preserve document structure
* Extract metadata:
  - Title, author, date
  - Source, category
  - Tags, keywords;

:**5. Document Analysis**
----
* Analyze document length
* Identify document type
* Detect language
* Extract entities
  (Names, dates, locations)
* Identify key sections
  (Headers, paragraphs)
* Analyze document quality
* Check readability
* Identify tables/figures
* Parse document hierarchy;

:**6. Text Chunking Strategy**
----
* Define chunking method:
  - Fixed-size chunks
  - Sentence-based chunks
  - Paragraph-based chunks
  - Semantic chunks
  - Sliding window
  - Recursive chunking
* Set chunk size
  (e.g., 256, 512, 1024 tokens)
* Set chunk overlap
  (e.g., 10-20% overlap)
* Preserve context boundaries
* Consider LLM context window
* Balance granularity vs context;

:**7. Document Chunking**
----
* Split documents into chunks
* Apply overlap strategy
* Maintain chunk metadata:
  - Source document ID
  - Chunk position/index
  - Parent document info
  - Timestamp
* Preserve semantic coherence
* Handle edge cases:
  - Tables spanning chunks
  - Code blocks
  - Lists
* Assign unique chunk IDs
* Store chunk relationships;

:**8. Chunk Enhancement**
----
* Add contextual information
* Prepend document title/summary
* Add section headers to chunks
* Include document metadata
* Generate chunk summaries
* Add keywords/tags
* Create hypothetical questions
  (for HyDE - Hypothetical
   Document Embeddings)
* Enrich with domain info
* Add temporal context;

:**9. Embedding Model Selection**
----
* Choose embedding model:
  - OpenAI (text-embedding-3)
  - Sentence Transformers
  - Cohere Embed
  - Google (Vertex AI)
  - Custom fine-tuned models
* Consider embedding dimensions
  (e.g., 384, 768, 1536)
* Evaluate model quality
* Check domain compatibility
* Review pricing/licensing
* Test model performance
* Consider multilingual needs;

:**10. Embedding Generation**
----
* Initialize embedding model
* Process chunks in batches
* Generate embeddings:
  - Convert text to vectors
  - Normalize embeddings
  - Handle long texts
* Store embeddings
* Link embeddings to chunks
* Handle embedding errors
* Track embedding metadata
* Calculate embedding stats
* Monitor resource usage;

:**11. Vector Database Selection**
----
* Choose vector database:
  - Pinecone
  - Weaviate
  - Qdrant
  - Milvus
  - ChromaDB
  - FAISS
  - Elasticsearch
  - pgvector (PostgreSQL)
* Consider features:
  - Similarity search algorithms
  - Filtering capabilities
  - Scalability
  - Performance
  - Cost
  - Hybrid search support
  - Metadata filtering;

:**12. Vector Database Setup**
----
* Initialize database
* Create collections/indices
* Configure index parameters:
  - Distance metric
    (Cosine, Euclidean, Dot Product)
  - Index type
    (HNSW, IVF, Flat)
  - Dimension size
* Set up sharding/partitioning
* Configure replication
* Set up access controls
* Optimize for query patterns
* Configure backups;

:**13. Data Indexing**
----
* Upload embeddings to vector DB
* Store chunk text/metadata
* Create searchable indices
* Batch insert for efficiency
* Handle indexing errors
* Verify data integrity
* Monitor indexing progress
* Optimize index structure
* Create metadata filters
* Build hybrid indices
  (if using keyword search);

:**14. Query Processing Pipeline**
----
* Receive user query
* Validate query input
* Apply query preprocessing:
  - Clean query text
  - Normalize text
  - Remove noise
  - Handle special chars
* Detect query intent
* Identify query type
  (Factual, Analytical, etc.)
* Extract query entities
* Log query metadata;

:**15. Query Expansion & Rewriting**
----
* Expand query with synonyms
* Add related terms
* Rephrase ambiguous queries
* Generate sub-queries
* Handle acronyms
* Add domain-specific terms
* Use query templates
* Generate multiple variants
* Apply spelling correction;

:**16. Query Embedding**
----
* Use same embedding model
  (as document embeddings)
* Generate query embedding vector
* Normalize query vector
* Handle multi-part queries
* Cache query embeddings
* Validate embedding quality;

:**17. Retrieval Strategy**
----
* Configure retrieval parameters:
  - Top-K results (e.g., 5-20)
  - Similarity threshold
  - Distance metric
* Choose retrieval method:
  - Dense retrieval (vectors only)
  - Sparse retrieval (keywords)
  - Hybrid retrieval (both)
* Apply metadata filters:
  - Date ranges
  - Document types
  - Categories
  - Access permissions
* Configure reranking;

:**18. Vector Search Execution**
----
* Perform similarity search
* Query vector database
* Apply distance calculations
* Retrieve top-K candidates
* Get similarity scores
* Fetch associated metadata
* Apply filtering
* Handle search errors
* Track search latency
* Log search results;

:**19. Reranking (Optional)**
----
* Apply reranking models:
  - Cross-encoders
  - Cohere Rerank
  - Custom scoring
* Calculate relevance scores
* Consider recency
* Apply business rules
* Boost by metadata
* Combine multiple signals
* Reorder results
* Filter low-quality results;

:**20. Context Assembly**
----
* Retrieve chunk texts
* Order by relevance score
* Deduplicate similar chunks
* Group by source document
* Format retrieved context
* Add source attribution
* Limit context length
  (fit LLM context window)
* Add metadata (title, source)
* Structure context clearly
* Preserve context hierarchy;

:**21. Context Quality Check**
----
* Verify context relevance
* Check for contradictions
* Validate information freshness
* Ensure sufficient coverage
* Check context diversity
* Filter irrelevant chunks
* Validate source quality
* Assess completeness;

if (Context\nQuality\nSufficient?) then (No)
  :**Fallback Strategy**
  ----
  * Expand search parameters
  * Try alternative queries
  * Use broader filters
  * Increase top-K
  * Return partial results
  * Notify user of limitations;
else (Yes)
endif

:**22. Prompt Construction**
----
* Design RAG prompt template
* Add system instructions
* Insert retrieved context:
  - Format context clearly
  - Add source citations
  - Number references
* Add user query
* Include guidelines:
  - Use only provided context
  - Cite sources
  - Admit unknown info
* Set output format
* Add constraints/rules
* Optimize prompt length;

:**23. LLM Integration**
----
* Select LLM:
  - GPT-4, Claude, Gemini
  - Open-source (Llama, Mistral)
* Configure LLM parameters:
  - Temperature (0.0-0.3 for factual)
  - Max tokens
  - Top-p
  - Stop sequences
* Set up API connection
* Handle authentication
* Configure timeout/retries;

:**24. LLM Response Generation**
----
* Send prompt to LLM
* Include retrieved context
* Handle streaming (optional)
* Monitor token usage:
  - Context tokens
  - Query tokens
  - Response tokens
* Track generation time
* Handle LLM errors
* Implement fallbacks
* Log API calls;

if (LLM Request\nSuccessful?) then (No)
  :Handle Error;
  stop
else (Yes)
endif

:**25. Response Post-Processing**
----
* Extract LLM response
* Parse citations/references
* Format response:
  - Add markdown
  - Structure sections
  - Format code blocks
* Extract source links
* Validate response format
* Apply text cleanup
* Check response length
* Add metadata;

:**26. Citation & Source Linking**
----
* Map citations to sources
* Add source URLs/links
* Include document titles
* Add page numbers/sections
* Format references
* Create footnotes/endnotes
* Validate citation accuracy
* Provide access to sources;

:**27. Response Validation**
----
* Check factual accuracy
* Verify citations match sources
* Detect hallucinations
* Compare with retrieved context
* Validate logical consistency
* Check for contradictions
* Assess answer completeness
* Apply content moderation;

if (Response\nValid?) then (No)
  :**Regenerate Response**
  ----
  * Adjust prompt
  * Modify context
  * Change LLM parameters
  * Try fallback strategy;
  detach
else (Yes)
endif

:**28. Response Delivery**
----
* Format final response
* Add source references
* Include confidence score
* Add metadata:
  - Response time
  - Sources used
  - Number of chunks
* Return to user
* Support follow-up queries
* Enable feedback collection;

:**29. User Feedback Collection**
----
* Collect explicit feedback:
  - Thumbs up/down
  - Star ratings
  - Comments
* Track implicit signals:
  - Follow-up queries
  - Time on page
  - Source clicks
* Log feedback data
* Associate with query/response
* Store user interactions;

:**30. Response Evaluation**
----
* Measure retrieval quality:
  - Precision@K
  - Recall@K
  - MRR (Mean Reciprocal Rank)
  - NDCG (Normalized DCG)
* Measure generation quality:
  - Faithfulness
  - Answer relevance
  - Context precision
  - Context recall
* Track user satisfaction
* Monitor answer accuracy
* Analyze failure cases;

:**31. Performance Monitoring**
----
* Track system metrics:
  - Query latency (total)
  - Retrieval time
  - LLM generation time
  - End-to-end latency
* Monitor throughput
* Track error rates
* Monitor resource usage:
  - Vector DB performance
  - LLM API usage
  - Cache hit rates
* Set up alerts
* Track cost per query;

:**32. Quality Analysis**
----
* Review low-rated responses
* Analyze retrieval failures
* Identify knowledge gaps
* Check embedding quality
* Review query patterns
* Analyze edge cases
* Identify common errors
* Monitor hallucinations
* Track context relevance;

:**33. Knowledge Base Updates**
----
* Identify outdated content
* Add new documents
* Update existing documents
* Remove obsolete content
* Track document versions
* Handle incremental updates
* Maintain consistency
* Update metadata;

if (New Documents\nAvailable?) then (Yes)
  :**Process New Documents**
  ----
  * Ingest new content
  * Generate embeddings
  * Update vector database
  * Refresh indices
  * Validate updates
  * Test retrieval quality;
  
else (No)
endif

:**34. System Optimization**
----
* Optimize chunking strategy
* Fine-tune embedding models
* Improve retrieval parameters
* Optimize reranking
* Refine prompts
* Adjust LLM parameters
* Optimize vector DB config
* Improve caching
* Reduce latency
* Control costs;

:**35. Continuous Improvement**
----
* Analyze usage patterns
* Update prompt templates
* Improve data quality
* Add new data sources
* Enhance preprocessing
* Optimize infrastructure
* Update evaluation metrics
* Implement A/B testing
* Review cost efficiency
* Plan feature enhancements;

:Maintain RAG System;

stop

